==Battleground==
*9 [[Ghost Doge]]s spawn, delay 6.67~20 seconds<sup>200f~600f</sup>.
*6 [[Ghost Snache]]s spawn, delay 13.33~26.67 seconds<sup>400f~800f</sup>.
*3 [[Ghost Baa Baa]]s spawn, delay 26.67~53.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,600f</sup>.
*1 [[Hermit Peng]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*1 [[Lione Hippoe]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Lione Hippoe]] spawns after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Samurai Doggy]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Ghost Doge]]s spawn, delay 6.67~20 seconds<sup>200f~600f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Ghost Snache]]s spawn, delay 13.33~26.67 seconds<sup>400f~800f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Ghost Baa Baa]]s spawn, delay 26.67~53.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,600f</sup>.
**2 [[Bearkini]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
**2 [[Dashing Face]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage may be harder for new players than its predecessors, but the only real requirement to beat it is obtaining all of [[Empire of Cats]]' important [[Treasure]]s. The gist of the stage is stacking [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Leg Cats]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cats]] before the boss wave and more on Samurai Doggy before the Bearkinis and Leggsies become an issue, while maintaining your defenses with [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cat]], [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Whale Cat]], and [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Mythical Titan Cat]]. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] and other ranged attackers such as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] and [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]] are not required to beat the stage but help immensely.

